<?xml version="1.0"?>
<rdf:RDF xmlns="https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498/instances#"
     xml:base="https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498/instances"
     xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#"
     xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#"
     xmlns:xml="http://www.w3.org/XML/1998/namespace"
     xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
     xmlns:bibo="http://purl.org/ontology/bibo/"
     xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#"
     xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#"
     xmlns:vann="http://purl.org/vocab/vann/"
     xmlns:terms="http://purl.org/dc/terms/"
     xmlns:iso7498="https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498#">
    <owl:Ontology rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498/instances">
        <owl:versionIRI rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498/instances/1.0.0"/>
        <owl:imports rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498"/>
        <terms:created rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2026-08-17</terms:created>
        <terms:creator>TODO: author name, ORCID</terms:creator>
        <terms:description xml:lang="en">Named individuals for the ISO/IEC 7498-1 ontology design pattern: the seven layers of the reference model, the protocol data units practice names per layer, common technologies of industrial communication, and the quality of service parameters.

They are kept apart from the pattern so that the terminology and the vocabulary can be maintained separately. A model importing only the pattern gets the classes; one importing this file gets the vocabulary as well, and need not declare that MQTT is an application layer technology for itself.</terms:description>
        <terms:license rdf:resource="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"/>
        <terms:publisher>TODO: institution</terms:publisher>
        <terms:title xml:lang="en">ISO/IEC 7498-1 Pattern: Named Individuals</terms:title>
        <bibo:status xml:lang="en">Draft</bibo:status>
        <vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>iso7498-inst</vann:preferredNamespacePrefix>
        <vann:preferredNamespaceUri>https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498/instances#</vann:preferredNamespaceUri>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Three groups of individual, with different standing.

The seven layers are normative: ISO/IEC 7498-1, 6.1.2 enumerates them and gives each a number.

The protocol data units and the technologies are conventional. Frame, packet, and segment do not occur in the standard, and 1.3 states that it implies no particular technology. They are supplied because an engineering model needs them and because naming them once keeps models comparable. The list of technologies is open by design.

The quality of service parameters follow 7.4.4 for the four the standard names, and extend beyond it where practice requires, which is marked at the affected individuals.</rdfs:comment>
        <owl:versionInfo>1.0.0</owl:versionInfo>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


